-- v22-era seed fixture for the migration_upgrade integration test.
--
-- Rows shaped to the schema at schema_version=22 (post-org-chart, pre-roster).
-- BLOB ids use stable hex constants so the test can re-derive them if needed:
--   tenant_id   X'aa…0N'   (N = 1,2,3)
--   workspace   X'bb…0N'
--   session     X'cc…NN'
--   skill       X'dd…NN'
--   memory      X'ee…NN'
--
-- Audit chain rows are NOT seeded here — the test builds them in Rust
-- so the sha256 parent_hash → self_hash linkage is computed from the
-- same algorithm used by argo_audit::sink (`sha256(parent || kind ||
-- 0x00 || payload)`).

-- 3 tenants → 3 workspaces.

-- 5 workers across the 3 tenants. Worker schema at v22 includes fs_root (v20).

-- 20 sessions: 7 on workspace-a, 7 on workspace-b, 6 on workspace-c.

-- 10 skills.

-- 30 memory_entry rows. v22-era columns: id, workspace_id, file, body,
-- learned_in, learned_at, superseded_by, hash, vertical_id (v10), layer
-- (v13, NOT NULL DEFAULT 'recent'), tenant_id (v13), worker_id (v13),
-- memory_scope (v13). Only required columns listed below — the rest
-- get defaults or NULL.
